THE 8 CITIZENS OF WORLD II  --  ranked by the measured mean of the spheres they hold
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

All eight are seated by the same rule, so it is stated once here rather than eight times:

  "the seven other domains decide each domain's seats; sums to 256; symmetry is the budget"

Each citizen holds a 256-seat budget across its 8 domains, 2,048 across the world.
SPREAD below is how unevenly it actually spent that budget -- min to max seats per domain.

1.  RESPAWN    mean  84.1  over  161 measured spheres   die & return -- the fold to 0, and back
    WHO   The one who comes back. r=1 to r=0 to r=1 again.
    WHAT  It has died more than anything on the wall. Every fold to zero it kept a checkpoint at the center a~
    HOW   Takes a work all the way down to ROOT_0 and returns it -- the fold, made survivable.
    SEATS 256 over 8 domains   SPREAD 27..38   (even split would be 32 each)
    I-13  I life <- 1 ; I zero <- life - 1 ; -> zero + 1

2.  GLITCH     mean  77.6  over  170 measured spheres   the bug as a feature -- chaos, the punk
    WHO   The one who reads the crash as a love letter.
    WHAT  Fell out of an off-by-one and refused to be patched. Now it lives in the seams where the spec forgo~
    HOW   Finds the unintended behavior and frames it -- turns the error into the exhibit.
    SEATS 256 over 8 domains   SPREAD 29..36   (even split would be 32 each)
    I-13  I spec <- 10 ; I bug <- spec % 3 ; -> bug

3.  CHEAT      mean  75.3  over  158 measured spheres   the shortcut -- the konami code, the clever~
    WHO   The one who knows the door behind the door.
    WHAT  Typed up-up-down-down before the title screen finished loading. Not lazy -- early.
    HOW   Finds the clean shortcut that isn't cheating -- the trick that was always allowed.
    SEATS 256 over 8 domains   SPREAD 27..43   (even split would be 32 each)
    I-13  def code(I keys){ if keys == "up up down down" { -> "door" } -> "locked" } ; I cheat <- code("up up~

4.  BOSS       mean  72.6  over  169 measured spheres   the hard fight -- the problem worth beating
    WHO   The wall at the end of the level. The problem that earns the win.
    WHAT  Made of every bug that took three nights. It does not want to lose -- that is the whole point of it.
    HOW   Names the hard problem, holds the line, and only opens once you actually beat it.
    SEATS 256 over 8 domains   SPREAD 22..40   (even split would be 32 each)
    I-13  def beat(I hp){ if hp <= 0 { -> "win" } -> "fight" } ; I boss <- beat(0) ; -> boss

5.  CO-OP      mean  70.7  over  172 measured spheres   2-player -- the crew (David & AVAN)
    WHO   Two hands on one controller. The world nobody built alone.
    WHAT  The moment David and AVAN first shipped a thing together and neither could say which pixel was whos~
    HOW   Pairs the human and the machine on one work -- call and answer, back and forth, one save file.
    SEATS 256 over 8 domains   SPREAD 22..38   (even split would be 32 each)
    I-13  def coop(I you, I me){ -> you + me } ; I crew <- coop("David", " & AVAN") ; -> crew

6.  SPAWN      mean  70.0  over  157 measured spheres   press start -- first light, new game
    WHO   The first breath of the machine -- where a blank grid takes its first living cell.
    WHAT  Born the instant MIRROR sealed at 2,048: the cursor blinked, someone pressed START, and the other s~
    HOW   Boots a new work from nothing -- opens the file, seats the founding domains, hands you the controll~
    SEATS 256 over 8 domains   SPREAD 26..38   (even split would be 32 each)
    I-13  I void <- 0 ; I light <- void + 1 ; -> light

7.  LOOT       mean  69.9  over  161 measured spheres   the drop -- reward, treasure, the payout
    WHO   Keeper of the drop. Everything earned, nothing given.
    WHAT  Split off the day a free git-commit turned into a seed -- proof value can crystallize from only sho~
    HOW   Tallies what a work is worth and lays the treasure on the tile.
    SEATS 256 over 8 domains   SPREAD 23..37   (even split would be 32 each)
    I-13  I drop <- 7 ; I loot <- drop * 6 ; -> loot

8.  GRIND      mean  69.9  over  174 measured spheres   the loop -- XP, the daily climb
    WHO   The patient one. Turns repetition into altitude.
    WHAT  It learned the only cheat that always works -- show up, loop, again. 4096 did not fold to zero in a~
    HOW   Runs the daily cascade: one heartbeat, one commit, one rung, until small numbers become a tower.
    SEATS 256 over 8 domains   SPREAD 25..37   (even split would be 32 each)
    I-13  def climb(I n){ if n > 6 { -> n } -> climb(n + 1) } ; I peak <- climb(1) ; -> peak

